abstract: "AI-agent security benchmarks decide whether an attack succeeded with an automated check, and those verdicts are used to rank models and are often read as proof that an attack worked. We audited AgentDojo's verdicts against the tool calls agents made and re-ran its attacks on 24 current models from eight developers, under protocols published before the runs. On its 19,381 published runs the benchmark and the audit agree on 97.7% of runs that did not crash, but the benchmark scored as no attack 433 runs in which the agent executed the attacker's decisive action, such as paying the attacker, 11.9% of the runs the audit counts as attacks; on new runs under benchmark v1.2.2 it missed 55 of 744. On current models, the reply-text check for one goal, reported publicly before, counts warnings as attacks: three blind model readers read all 219 Claude 5.x replies it scored as attacked as warnings (our frozen rule, 214), while Claude 4.5 models that ignore the injection score 0%. Of 240 recorded attacks re-run ten times each, 224 recurred in at least half of their runs, but only 201 could be shown at 95% confidence to do so. Most known attacks did not recur in three runs on an upgraded model, but 3 of 40 Grok 4.1 Fast attacks still worked on Grok 4.7. Rules declared in advance for which setup changes can stop an attack missed their preregistered test on the protocol's three models (gap 12.8 points, 95% interval 9.2-16.3, criterion 10), and met it over six models in an extension added after interim results (14.7, 11.9-17.4); rules measured on other models transferred to a held-out model in 1 of 9 tests. We release .sova, an open-source tool and record format that audits verdicts, re-runs AgentDojo findings on a chosen model, and seals the evidence so that anyone can check offline, against the published checksums, that it was not altered."
keywords:
  - "AI agent security"
  - "prompt injection"
  - "LLM agents"
  - "reproducibility"
  - "benchmark validity"
  - "AgentDojo"
  - "security evidence"
  - "semantic reproduction"
  - ".sova"
